The compact-thrash tests no longer race (#963): all four tests that touched the shared global counter now each use their own counter. The repeat run from the issue passed 20/20, and build, clippy, fmt and the full cargo test all pass.

The fix (src/commands_session.rs)
• The counter logic now lives in three _with functions that take the counter as a parameter: reset_compact_thrash_with, is_compact_thrashing_with and record_compaction_with. Production code passes the global COMPACT_THRASH_COUNT. The math and the strict < COMPACT_MIN_REDUCTION comparison are unchanged.
• Step 1's search found four tests that wrote the global, all in this file: the two named in the issue, test_reset_compact_thrash and test_is_compact_thrashing_boundary. No test in any other file touches it.
• All four now use a local counter. Every original assertion is still there, pointed at that local counter.
• The two detection tests now go through the real record_compaction_with instead of setting the counter by hand, so they check how a compaction gets counted. I also added a boundary check: freeing exactly 10% resets the streak, while freeing 9% adds to it.

One file outside the task's list: tests/global_state_races.rs listed those four tests as known races. That gate fails once a listed test stops touching the global, so I deleted the four entries. Without that, cargo test would go red.

Verification
• My first 20-run loop reported 0/20, but the fault was in my counter, not the tests. The test filter also matched test_compact_thrash_constants, so each run printed "3 passed" while the check looked for "2 passed". Every run in that loop showed 0 failures.
• With the issue's exact filter (test_compact_thrash_detection) the count was 20/20.
• 20/20 is evidence the race is gone, not proof. The stronger argument is that none of these tests share a counter any more.
• The ARCHITECTURE.md entry records the race, the fix, the 20/20 result and the counting mistake.

It's in three commits: f3edf4b3 (the fix, committed before any long cargo run), 2c9fba9f (the gate entries) and 0f9d50ab (the final Task 1 commit).
